From: zyi
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: zero3w: standby_param node and DRAM parameters

The E902 SCP parses two things from the FDT it is pointed at
(RTC_DTB_BASE_STORE_REG -> 0x44000000 in our boot flow, the kernel DTB
loaded there by boot.cmd):

1. /standby_param (resolved through the aliases entry) -- power-domain
   bitmaps for deep sleep and osc24m-on. Missing it makes the SCP warn
   "WRN:no standby_param" and keep every rail on during deep sleep.
   Add the node with osc24m-on = <1> (keep the 26 MHz DCXO running, the
   firmware default) and deliberately NO rail bitmaps yet: zero bitmaps
   mean "switch nothing off", the safe configuration while the wake-up
   path is still being debugged. Rail-off values can be copied from the
   A733 pro3 reference board.dts once deep suspend survives a cycle.

2. /dram dram_para00..31 -- the DRAM parameter array the SCP's
   dram_power_save_process/dram_power_up_process (libar100s.a) consume
   for the self-refresh save/restore. Without them the whole array
   parses to zero and the debug SCP console went silent right after
   "the first time ddr standby" and the board never woke up. Values are
   the set boot0 itself trains with: the board carries 4 GiB LPDDR5 and
   boot0_sdcard_orangepizero3w.fex selects its header set ("vaild
   para:4  select dram para0", "DRAM Type =9"), copied word for word
   from boot0 offset 0x38, with dram_para07 set to boot0's post-autoscan
   value 0x10001001 (4 GiB size field; boot log "para1 = a0fa, para2 =
   10001001, dram_tpr13 = 65"). The generic sys_config.fex [dram_para]
   block is LPDDR4 (type 8) and must not be used: restoring with it
   leaves DRAM unreadable and CPU0 never resumes (board test 2026-10-01).

Array index -> struct field mapping is __dram_para_t in the arisc
source (dram.h): 00 dram_clk, 01 dram_type, 02 dx_odt, 03 dx_dri,
04 ca_dri, 05 para0, 06 para1, 07 para2, 08..21 mr*, 22..26 tpr0/1/2/3/6,
27..31 tpr10/11/12/13/14.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-orangepi-zero3w.dts	2026-09-30 01:32:27.600625708 +0800
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-orangepi-zero3w.dts	2026-09-30 01:32:27.613626397 +0800
@@ -11,6 +11,16 @@
 		arisc-config = &arisc_config;
 		pmu0 = &pmu0;
 		bat_supply = &bat_power_supply;
+		standby_param = &standby_param;
+	};
+
+	/*
+	 * Parsed by the E902 SCP (fdt_path_offset "standby_param") for the
+	 * deep-suspend power plan. No rail bitmaps yet: zero = switch nothing
+	 * off during deep sleep. osc24m-on=1 keeps the DCXO running.
+	 */
+	standby_param: standby_param {
+		osc24m-on = <1>;
 	};
 
 	reg_usb0_vbus: usb0-vbus {
@@ -4087,3 +4097,43 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/*
+ * DRAM parameters for the SCP's DRAM save/restore (index -> field mapping is
+ * __dram_para_t in the arisc source dram.h): boot0's own LPDDR5 set "para0"
+ * (boot0_sdcard_orangepizero3w.fex offset 0x38) with dram_para07 = boot0's
+ * post-autoscan 0x10001001 (4 GiB).
+ */
+&dram {
+	dram_para00 = <2400>;
+	dram_para01 = <9>;
+	dram_para02 = <0x0e0e0e0e>;
+	dram_para03 = <0x0f0f0f0f>;
+	dram_para04 = <0xec030e0f>;
+	dram_para05 = <0>;
+	dram_para06 = <0xa0fa>;
+	dram_para07 = <0x10001001>;
+	dram_para08 = <0>;
+	dram_para09 = <0>;
+	dram_para10 = <0>;
+	dram_para11 = <6>;
+	dram_para12 = <0>;
+	dram_para13 = <0>;
+	dram_para14 = <0>;
+	dram_para15 = <0x14>;
+	dram_para16 = <0x44>;
+	dram_para17 = <0>;
+	dram_para18 = <0x28>;
+	dram_para19 = <0>;
+	dram_para20 = <6>;
+	dram_para21 = <0>;
+	dram_para22 = <0x4040>;
+	dram_para23 = <0>;
+	dram_para24 = <0x170b0703>;
+	dram_para25 = <0x3800>;
+	dram_para26 = <0x3514>;
+	dram_para27 = <0x325f0000>;
+	dram_para28 = <0>;
+	dram_para29 = <0>;
+	dram_para30 = <0x65>;
+	dram_para31 = <0>;
+};
